content:
{{Transcript|npc}}

== On the Lady Zay after docking at Lunar Isle ==
* '''Player:''' I feel a little sea-sick from this travelling.
* ''' 'Birds-Eye' Jack:''' Well there's a good remedy for that.
* '''Player:''' There is?
* ''' 'Birds-Eye' Jack:''' Yes.
* '''Player:''' What?
* ''' 'Birds-Eye' Jack:''' Swim.
* '''Player:''' Oh HA HA. Thanks for the help!
* ''' 'Birds-Eye' Jack:''' My pleasure.
* '''Player:''' I was being sarcastic.
* ''' 'Birds-Eye' Jack:''' I know. So was I.
* {{tact|end}}

== At Lunar Isle bank ==
* {{tselect|What would you like to talk about?}}
* {{topt|Using the bank}}
** {{tselect|What would you like to say?}}
** {{topt|I'd like to access my bank account, please.}}
*** '''Player:''' I'd like to access my bank account, please.
*** {{tact|Bank interface opens.}}
** {{topt|I'd like to collect items.}}
*** '''Player:''' I'd like to collect items.
*** {{tact|Grand Exchange collection interface opens.}}
** {{topt|I'd like to check my PIN settings.}}
*** '''Player:''' I'd like to check my PIN settings.
*** {{tact|Pin settings interface opens.}}
** {{topt|What is this place?}}
*** '''Player:''' What is this place?
*** ''' 'Bird's-Eye' Jack:''' This is a branch of the Bank of Gielinor. We have branches in many towns.
*** '''Player:''' And what do you do?
*** ''' 'Bird's-Eye' Jack:''' We will look after your items and money for you. Leave your valuables with us if you want to keep them safe.
*** {{tact|end}}
* {{topt|Cyrisus in the mine}}
** '''Player:''' Hi.
** ''' 'Bird's-Eye' Jack:''' How's Cyrisus? Where is he?
** '''Player:''' He's fine now. Back to full health.
** ''' 'Bird's-Eye' Jack:''' Good, I'm pleased.
** '''Player:''' No problem.
** ''' 'Bird's-Eye' Jack:''' Don't think that this means I like you now!
** '''Player:''' Look at my face.
** ''' 'Bird's-Eye' Jack:''' Yes? What about it.
** '''Player:''' Does it look like I care?
** ''' 'Bird's-Eye' Jack:''' Not really.
** '''Player:''' Well, there you go.
** {{tact|end}}

{{Transcript|npc}}

==Standard dialogue== 
===Before [[Tower of Life]]===
* '''Player:''' What's going on?
* '''<nowiki>'Black-eye':</nowiki>''' Ah, we be building this 'ere tower. Lookin' good ain't it?
* '''Player:''' It does look pretty impressive, but what are you doing hanging around?
* '''<nowiki>'Black-eye':</nowiki>''' Tea break, naturally.
* '''Player:''' Naturally. Not sure why I asked.
* '''<nowiki>'Black-eye':</nowiki>''' Fancy some?
* '''Player:''' Tea? Sure.
* '''<nowiki>'Black-eye':</nowiki>''' You'll find a kettle in the box to the-
* '''Player:''' Erm...yeah...no...sorry...gotta go.
* {{tact|end}}

===After [[Tower of Life]]===
* '''Player:''' Say, that's a nice helmet.
* {{tcond|Player does not have a [[Hard hat]] in bank or inventory:}}
** '''<nowiki>'Black-eye'</nowiki>:''' Why, thanks.
** '''Player:''' I was just wondering if you might be able to help me out with one?
** '''<nowiki>'Black-eye'</nowiki>:''' Always glad to help a budding builder. But first, prove your Construction knowledge by answering some questions.
** '''<nowiki>'Black-eye'</nowiki>:''' How many nails does it take to make a rocking chair?
** {{tselect|Select an option}}
** {{topt|One}}
*** '''Player:''' One?
*** '''<nowiki>'Black-eye'</nowiki>:''' One? How do you suppose you'd use a single nail?
*** {{tact|end}}
** {{topt|Five}}
*** '''Player:''' Five?
*** '''<nowiki>'Black-eye'</nowiki>:''' Nope. Keep guessing!
*** {{tact|end}}
** {{topt|Three}}
*** '''Player:''' Three?
*** '''<nowiki>'Black-eye'</nowiki>:''' Bingo! Okay, now what takes 3 planks, 3 cloths and 3 nails to make, and helps remove light from a room?
*** {{tselect|Select an option}}
*** {{topt|Torn curtains}}
**** '''Player:''' Torn curtains?
**** '''<nowiki>'Black-eye'</nowiki>:''' Nice one. Last question: I like fish and I want to put some in my garden, but I need a special water feature. What materials would I require?
**** {{tselect|Select an option}}
**** {{topt|8 clay pieces and 3 limestone bricks}}
***** '''Player:''' 8 clay pieces and 3 limestone bricks?
***** '''<nowiki>'Black-eye'</nowiki>:''' Oh, and you were so close!
***** {{tact|end}}
**** {{topt|10 clay pieces}}
***** '''Player:''' 10 clay pieces?
***** '''<nowiki>'Black-eye'</nowiki>:''' That's it! You seem to know your stuff. I got a spare helmet from a builder that died on... I mean, err, had to leave the job for greener pastures.
***** '''Player:''' Greener pastures?
***** '''Player:''' Fair enough.
***** {{tact|receives=Hard hat}}
***** '''Player:''' Wait a minute! Is there blood on this helmet?
***** '''<nowiki>'Black-eye'</nowiki>:''' Erm, no, that's just, erm, paint. Yes, paint! That's what it is!
***** '''Player:''' Oh, okay. Thanks. Bye.
***** '''<nowiki>'Black-eye'</nowiki>:''' Ha, gullible fool.
***** '''Player:''' What?
***** '''<nowiki>'Black-eye'</nowiki>:''' Nothing.
***** {{tact|end}}
**** {{topt|10 limestone bricks}}
***** '''Player:''' 10 limestone bricks?
***** '''<nowiki>'Black-eye'</nowiki>:''' Guess again.
***** {{tact|end}}
*** {{topt|A brown rug}}
**** '''Player:''' A brown rug?
**** '''<nowiki>'Black-eye'</nowiki>:''' Of course, because that's what everyone needs - a rug up at their window.
**** {{tact|end}}
*** {{topt|Opulent curtains}}
**** '''Player:''' Opulent curtains?
**** '''<nowiki>'Black-eye'</nowiki>:''' Those curtains are not going to be in any way opulent, matey.
**** {{tact|end}}
* {{tcond|Player has [[Hard hat]] in bank:}}
** '''<nowiki>'Black-eye':</nowiki>''' Thank you - just as nice as the one in your bank!
** {{tact|end}}
* {{tcond|Player has [[Hard hat]] in inventory:}}
** '''<nowiki>'Black-eye'</nowiki>:''' Yes - just as nice as the one you're carrying I'd say.
** {{tact|end}}

{{Transcript|npc}}

==Standard dialogue==
* ''''Squawking' Steve Beanie:''' Yarr! What will it be?
* {{tselect|Select an option}}
* {{topt|Let's see what you have.}}
** '''Player:''' Let's see what you have.
** ''''Squawking' Steve Beanie:''' Aye!
** {{tact|opens=The Pandemonium (Pub)}}
* {{topt|Any word from Old Grog?}}
** '''Player:''' Any word from Old Grog?
** ''''Squawking' Steve Beanie:''' Nothing yet, you scallywag, but keep checking in. I'm sure he'll have something soon. Now, what will it be?
** {{tact|other}}
* {{topt|Got any work that needs doing here?}}
** '''Player:''' Got any work that needs doing here?
** ''''Squawking' Steve Beanie:''' Well, it just so happens that I'm looking for a rough, tough, piratical type for an adventure on the high seas!
** ''''Squawking' Steve Beanie:''' And I'm happy to say...
** {{tact|Continues in [[Transcript:Prying Times]]}}
* {{topt|Could you tell me about the Pandemonium's one rule?}}
** '''Player:''' Could you tell me about the Pandemonium's one rule?
** ''''Squawking' Steve Beanie:''' Avast! The mainland kingdoms have no authority here. Their laws do not apply. Instead, we just have our one rule that keeps the Pandemonium afloat: Never disrespect your fellow patron.
** ''''Squawking' Steve Beanie:''' We don't care who you are. Indeed, pirates and customs officers can enjoy a drink here, side by side. Savvy?
** '''Player:''' So anyone is welcome here as long as they don't commit an offense against any of the other patrons?
** ''''Squawking' Steve Beanie:''' Yarr! You've got it! Now, what will it be?
** {{tact|other}}
* {{topt|Nothing, thanks.}}
** '''Player:''' Nothing, thanks.
** ''''Squawking' Steve Beanie:''' Shiver me timbers!
** {{tact|end}}

{{Transcript|npc}}
==Standard dialogue==
===Before [[Tower of Life]]===
* '''Player:''' Wow, that looks pretty heavy.
* '''<nowiki>'The Guns':</nowiki>''' Umpf! Yeah, mate...argghh...this is...umpf...hard work...
* '''Player:''' What would happen if I were to say...
* '''Player:''' 135
* '''Player:''' 25
* '''Player:''' 234
* '''Player:''' 2351...
* '''<nowiki>'The Guns':</nowiki>''' Stop! Stop! Humpf...I'll beat you to...urghh...a pulp!
* '''Player:''' Okay, okay! Don't cry!
* '''<nowiki>'The Guns':</nowiki>''' Why, I oughta...
* {{tact|end}}

===After [[Tower of Life]]===
* '''Player:''' What do you do when you're not lifting logs above your head?
* '''<nowiki>'The Guns':</nowiki>''' In my free time?
* '''Player:''' Yes.
* '''<nowiki>'The Guns':</nowiki>''' All sorts. I like...hummff...a good kebab and a cold beer down...urrghh...the pub. And for those quiet evenings...hurrr...
* '''<nowiki>'The Guns':</nowiki>''' A bit of needlepoint is always welcome.
* '''Player:''' I can honestly say you're a very original guy.
* {{tact|end}}

==Overhead dialogue==
===Below 5,000===
* '''<nowiki>'The Guns':</nowiki>''' {{overhead|1}}
* '''<nowiki>'The Guns':</nowiki>''' {{overhead|2}}
* {{tact|<nowiki>'The Guns'</nowiki> continues counting for several hours.}}
* '''<nowiki>'The Guns':</nowiki>''' {{overhead|4999}}
* '''<nowiki>'The Guns':</nowiki>''' {{overhead|5000}}

===Above 5,000===
* {{tact|'The Guns' will randomly lose count between 5,000 and 10,000:}}
* '''<nowiki>'The Guns':</nowiki>''' {{overhead|[xxxx]}}
* '''<nowiki>'The Guns':</nowiki>''' {{overhead|10012...15?}}
* '''<nowiki>'The Guns':</nowiki>''' {{overhead|Huh?}}
* '''<nowiki>'The Guns':</nowiki>''' {{overhead|Bah}}
* '''<nowiki>'The Guns':</nowiki>''' {{overhead|Start again!}}
* {{tact|above}}

{{Transcript|npc}}

==Standard dialogue==
* '''Player:''' Hi there. What is this place?
* '''<nowiki/>'Transmute' The Alchemist:''' Ah, this be the Tower of Life! Beautiful, isn't it?
* '''Player:''' I prefer ordinary houses.
* '''<nowiki/>'Transmute' The Alchemist:''' Pah, you have no taste.
* {{tact|end}}
{{DEFAULTSORT:Transmute The Alchemist}}

{{Transcript|npc}}

==Standard dialogue==
* '''1v1 Tournament Guide:''' Welcome to the Emir's Arena! Are you interested in 1v1 Tournaments? We organise ranked Tournaments here, or alternatively you can organise your own unranked Tournaments.
* {{tselect|Select an Option}}
* {{topt|What's a 1v1 Tournament?}}
** '''Player:''' What's a 1v1 Tournament?
** '''1v1 Tournament Guide:''' A group of fighters is divided into pairs of opponents, and they all fight their opponent. The winners of those fights proceed to the next round, where they're divided into pairs, and they each fight their new opponent.
** '''1v1 Tournament Guide:''' The number of surviving fighters is halved each time, until eventually only one person is left standing. They're the winner of the Tournament.
** {{tact|other}}
* {{topt|Ranked or unranked? What does that mean?}}
** '''Player:''' Ranked or unranked? What does that mean?
** '''1v1 Tournament Guide:''' Everyone has a rank. It's meant to indicate how good they are at fighting, compared to other people.
** '''1v1 Tournament Guide:''' In ranked fights, the winners gain rank and the losers lose rank. The Arena staff will decide who'll be fighting in each ranked Tournament, and send the invitations.
** '''1v1 Tournament Guide:''' But if you just want some casual fun, you can have an unranked Tournament, where no-one gains or loses rank. You can organise your own unranked Tournament, and decide for yourself who'll fight in it.
** '''1v1 Tournament Guide:''' Only the ranked fights offer access to the other rewards of the Arena.
** {{tact|other}}
* {{topt|How do I get invited into a Tournament?}}
** '''Player:''' How do I get invited into a Tournament?
** '''1v1 Tournament Guide:''' You'll need to sign up to a recruitment group...
** {{tbox|pic=Grouping icon.png|This is the icon for the {{colour|#7f0000|Grouping}} tab. Within it you'll find the {{colour|#7f0000|PvP Arena}} options.}}
** {{tbox|pic=Grouping icon.png|There, you can click {{colour|#7f0000|Find}} to seek the official group for ranked Tournaments. Alternatively, you could look for another player's group, for an unranked Tournament.}}
** {{tbox|pic=Grouping icon.png|Once you've found a suitable group for you, click {{colour|#7f0000|Sign up}} to sign up to it, and you'll be considered for an invitation to a Tournament, whenever one begins.}}
** '''1v1 Tournament Guide:''' You can carry on with your adventures while you're waiting for a Tournament to begin, since it may be a while before suitable fighters are available.
** {{tact|other}}
* {{topt|I want to organise my own Tournament.}}
** '''Player:''' I want to organise my own Tournament.
** '''1v1 Tournament Guide:''' Just use my Recruitment Board here to form your own recruitment group. Once you've got one, wait for other fighters to join it.
** {{tbox|pic=Grouping icon.png|This is the icon for the {{colour|#7f0000|Grouping}} tab. Once you've formed a recruitment group, you'll be able to control it there, via the {{colour|#7f0000|PvP Arena}} options.}}
** {{tbox|pic=Grouping icon.png|When you're ready to start, click {{colour|#7f0000|Start}} to summon your awaiting fighters. You'll need to be on a {{colour|#7f0000|PvP Arena world }} to start your Tournament.}}
** {{topt|What's a 1v1 Tournament?}}
*** {{tact|above}}
** {{topt|Ranked or unranked? What does that mean?}}
*** {{tact|above}}
** {{topt|How do I get invited into a Tournament?}}
*** {{tact|above}}
** {{topt|Okay, goodbye.}}
*** '''Player:''' Okay, goodbye.
*** {{tact|end}}
* {{topt|I'm okay, thanks.}}
** '''Player:''' I'm okay, thanks.
** {{tact|end}}

{{Transcript|event}}
{{Transcript list|Shanty Claws|Jack (Christmas 2013)|Jeff (child)|Jill}}

==Starting out==
===Speaking to Shanty Claws===
====Initial conversation====
* '''Player:''' What are you doing here?
* {{tcond|If the player isn't wearing a ring of Charos:}}
** '''Shanty Claws:''' 'Raise the mainsail and hoist the anchor...' Eh! Oh, the names 'Shanty'; 'Shanty Claws' to a landlubber like ye. And oi've some terrible news for yer deck-swabbin' ears.
** {{tact|continues}}
* {{tcond|If the player is wearing a ring of Charos:}}
** '''Shanty Claws:''' 'Raise the mainsail and hoist the anchor...' Eh! A fellow werewolf! I say; I never expected that, friend! Oh, the name's 'Shanty'; 'Shanty Claws' to a landlubber like ye. And oi've some terrible news for yer deck-swabbin' ears.
** {{tact|continues}}
* '''Player:''' Well, I don't really swab the deck with... Oh, never mind, please do go on!
* '''Shanty Claws:''' 'Splice the mainsail and shiver me timbers...' Ah yea, the news is of a disturbin' type so ye's best go ahead and prepare yerself, or the jelly in yer bones'll shrivel and yer'll end up a lifeless bag o' puss.
* '''Player:''' Er, I think I'll manage. Please continue; your story's 'enthralling'.
* '''Shanty Claws:''' It's the gublinch, ye see. The evil gublinch ain't too pleased, what with the recent snow. Right near their landlubbin' homes, it be. And these sweaty, smelly, warmth-loving critters, they's a tad sensitive to the cold.
* '''Shanty Claws:''' So they've childernapped the childerkins from hereabouts, forcin' 'em to stoke the fires in the gublinch caves!
* '''Player:''' Childernapped the childerkins? Why, that sounds terrible! What can I do to help?
* '''Shanty Claws:''' You's be needin' to ice them gublinch. Freeze 'em good and proper, like. Then you's gonna have to get 'em into these 'ere cages so's we can ship 'em off someplace else!
* '''Player:''' What's in it for me?
* '''Shanty Claws:''' Ahhh, a hard-nosed dealer who talks straight, that's what I like. For yer 'ard effort, I'll be willin' ta compensate ye. How's ye fancy a festive hat with a fancy nose décor, what I got on a recent raid to the north?
* '''Player:''' Let's see it then.
* '''Shanty Claws:''' Right you are!
* {{tact|pic=Reindeer hat detail.png|Shanty Claws shows you a strange looking hat with an accompanying nose decoration.}}
* '''Player:''' Is there anything else to sweeten the deal?
* '''Shanty Claws:''' Perhaps I can also tempt ye with a festive wintumber tree for yer player-owned house? it glitters fancifully in front of yer very eyes, though to plant it ye's needing to be on one them thar member's worlds and
* '''Shanty Claws:''' have a spot in yer garden in which plant it.{{sic}}
* '''Player:''' Eh? So I can plant this tree in the garden of my player-owned house?
* '''Shanty Claws:''' Aye, that's what I said, aye. And to give it ye, you'll need to be on a members' server. If yer interested just start filling these 'ere cages with gublinch and, when they's filled, come see me for yer rewards.
* '''Player:''' Hmmm, I'm not sure. I want to ask a few more questions first.
* {{topt|What are gublinch?}}
** '''Player:''' What are gublinch?
** '''Shanty Claws:''' 'Fire the port gun, stow the belayin' pin...let's haul anchor ye mornin'...' Ah... So yer back and asking about th' gublinch? They're foul goberlin-style beasties, what take pride in their stinky sweatyness. Though
** '''Shanty Claws:''' they's be little more than a pest. They're easy to get rid o' with them being so sensitive to th' chill. They's prefer more to live in them heated caverns and cook up a foul stink, than to do a second's worth o' work.
** {{tact|other}}
* {{topt|Where are these gublinch?}}
** '''Player:''' Where are these gublinch?
** '''Shanty Claws:''' '...haul the anchor, rig the mainsail...' Eh? Ah, th' gublinch have gone and nested themselves in, near the belching mountain.
** '''Player:''' D'you mean the volcano?
** '''Shanty Claws:''' Aye, [lad/lass], volcano is what I be meanin'. The south foot o' the same. They's be 'avin' a cavern there, but arm yerself wi' the chilly snowball ammo afore ye goes venturin' inside.
** {{tact|other}}
* {{topt|What do I get for getting rid of these gublinch?}}
** '''Player:''' What do I get for getting rid of these gublinch?
** '''Shanty Claws:''' '...a brig's too good, so keelhaul him in the mornin'...' Ah, direct, ye are, and to the point. Well,  me swarthy deck-swabber, perhaps I can tempt ye with a festive hat with a big nose décor, what I got on a recent raid in the
** '''Shanty Claws:''' north?
** '''Player:''' Let's see it then.
** '''Shanty Claws:''' Right you are!
** {{tbox|pic=Reindeer hat detail.png|Shanty Claws shows you a strange-looking hat with an accompanying nose decoration.}}
** '''Player:''' Is there anything else to sweeten the deal?
** '''Shanty Claws:''' Perhaps I can also tempt ye with a festive wintumber tree for yer player-owned house? It glitters fancifully in front of yer very eyes, though to plant it ye's needing to be on one them thar members' worlds and
** '''Shanty Claws:''' have a spot in yer garden in which to plant it.
** '''Player:''' Eh? So I can plant this tree in the garden of my player-owned house?
** '''Shanty Claws:''' Aye, that's what I said, aye. And to give it ye, you'll need to be on a members' server. If yer interested, just start filling these 'ere cages and, when ten are filled, come to me for yer rewards.
** {{tact|initial}}
* {{topt|Can you just tell me in a plain and simple way what I have to do?}}
** '''Player:''' Can you just tell me in a plain and simple way what I have to do?
** '''Shanty Claws:''' Certainly, [player name]. Local children have been kidnapped by creatures called gublinch. The gublinch cave is on the south side of the volcano. The gublinch are sensitive to cold, so use snowballs to freeze 'em.
** '''Shanty Claws:''' Ye'll find snowdrifts near the entrance to their cave. When ye's frozen a gublinch, bring it back 'ere an' place it in one o' these cages.
** '''Shanty Claws:''' In return for filling all ten cages, I'll give ye a reindeer hat and a members' only wintumber tree that you can plant in th' garden o' yer player-owned house.
** {{tact|initial}}
* {{topt|Okay, thanks.}}
** '''Player:''' Okay, thanks.
** {{tact|end}}

====Repeating conversation====
* '''Player:''' Hello again. What should I do?
* '''Shanty Claws:''' 'Swab the decks and raise the top mast...' Oh, sorry there, ye be wantin' to know what to do, but yer already going great guns, shipmate! Keep up the good work, you old sea-dog, and get them gublinch shards
* '''Shanty Claws:''' into them thar cages!
* {{tact|(Same options as above.)}}

====Searching gublinch cave entrance====
* {{tbox|You search the strange structure and find a notice attached.}}
* {{tbox|*DANGER: GUBLINCH* This 'ere notice be warnin' all landlubbers o' these 'ere gublinch, what lie in wait in their stinky cavern below. Any swashbucklin' sailor or cutlass-wieldin' pirate wi' an eye fer treasure should seek out Shanty Claws (sailor), Musa Point, On the Dock. Thankee kindly.}}
* {{tact|end}}

====Placing gublinch shards in the cage====
* {{mes|You place the shards in the cage.}}
* {{mes|The gublinch rattles the cage doors, but cannot escape.}}

====Using gublinch shards on Shanty Claws====
* '''Shanty Claws:''' '...bring me home to a dry-dock and a bottle of hock...' Hey there, ye need to put them thar shards into a cage so's to restrain the gublinch!
* {{tact|end}}

====Using any other item on Shanty Claws====
* '''Shanty Claws:''' '...skimming the sea with a sailor's heart, lofty and high...' Hey, whad'ya think yer doin! Go shove that in someone else's face!
* {{tact|end}}

===After caging all of the gublinch===
* '''Player:''' I think I've finished.
* '''Shanty Claws:''' '...to exotic places with fair winds blowing in our faces...' Aarghhh! Me first mate, [player name] - ye's done a grand job, [lad/lass], and stuffed them evil gublinch in them cages. Now, this salty sea-wolf can offer ye something to make yer 
* '''Shanty Claws:''' eyes light up like ye's seen a treasure chest, brimful o' the bootiest booty ye ever did see.
* {{tbox|pic=Reindeer hat detail.png|Shanty Claws shows you a reindeer hat with a matching flashing nose.}}
* '''Shanty Claws:''' Ol' Shanty's got another prize for ye that'll make yer landlubbin' heart beat full bore. Ye'll be needing a patch o' dirt for yer dry-docked ship for this.
* '''Player:''' Dry-docked ship? Oh, you mean a player-owned house? Okay, so I need to plant it in the garden?
* '''Shanty Claws:''' Aye, that's what ol' Shanty says. Let it fill yer heart wi' festive cheer.
* {{tbox|pic=Wintumber tree detail.png|Shanty Claws shows you a wintumber tree for your player-owned house.}}
* '''Shanty Claws:''' An' that's not all Shanty's got for ye. Wrap yer hands around this pile o' festive booty...
* {{tact|end}}

==Overhead dialogue==
* {{tact|Repeats in this order:}}
* '''Shanty Claws:''' {{overhead|'Sailing on the sea...happy as can be...'}}
* '''Shanty Claws:''' {{overhead|'...to exotic places...fair winds in our faces...'}}
* '''Shanty Claws:''' {{overhead|'...and we'll sink a drink  to our sailor ways...'}}
* '''Shanty Claws:''' {{overhead|'...polish ye cutlass's makes 'em rust-less...'}}
* '''Shanty Claws:''' {{overhead|'...a brig's too good, so keelhaul him in the mornin'...'}}

==Post-event==
===Shanty Claws===
* '''Shanty Claws:''' '...and we'll sink another drink to our sailor ways...' Eh? Arrrrgh. If it ain't me first mate, [player name], again. Ye have me heartiest thanks fer sortin' them thar gublinch, mate. If ye needs yer booty back, get yerself along to
* '''Shanty Claws:''' Diango - I've left supplies wi' him, so I have.
* {{tselect|Select an Option}}
* {{topt|What will happen to the gublinch now?}}
** '''Player:''' What will happen to the gublinch now?
** '''Shanty Claws:''' '...skimming the sea with a sailor's heart, lofty and high...' Arrgh, you be here again then, shipmate...and well you can ask about them thar gublinch. But a-fear ye not - they's be disposed of well, mark my words. And a
** '''Shanty Claws:''' sweaty, swarthy bunch o' critters they'll be in their new home, far from here!
** {{tact|other}}
* {{topt|What will you do now?}}
** '''Player:''' What will you do now?
** '''Shanty Claws:''' I'll probably go on a long sea voyage and compose some more shanties! Shanty by name, shanty by nature!
** '''Shanty Claws:''' '...rounding the cape, with good hope in our heart, that we'll find treasure for our chests...' Arggh me swarthy landlubber, I's be sailin' away afore long, matey, an' striking up a tune for me shipmates; with a wholesome
** '''Shanty Claws:''' shanty coursing the rigging, old Shanty Claws will make his way. Wringing a salty sea song from the adventurers we'll survive, the people we'll meet and the treasure we'll find.
** {{tact|other}}
* {{topt|Okay, thanks.}}
** '''Player:''' Okay, thanks.
** {{tact|end}}

===Childerken===
* '''Jack/Jeff/Jill:''' Thanks so much for saving us from those stinky gublinch. They were awful! I hope Shanty gave you somefing{{sic}} cool for your efforts.
* {{tact|end}}

===Trying to climb down into the Gublinch cave===
* {{tbox|The cavern is empty of gublinch now; there's no need to go down there.}}
* {{tact|end}}

===Searching the cave entrance===
* {{tbox|You search the strange structure but find nothing.}}
* {{tact|end}}

{{2013 Christmas event}}

{{Transcript|event}}
{{Transcript list|Easter Bunny}}

==Starting out==
* '''Easter Bunny:''' Oh thank goodness you've come, [player name]. I've really made a mess of it this year.
* '''Player:''' What's happened?
* '''Easter Bunny:''' Last year I tried to hypnotise the bunnies to deliver the eggs to the children.
* '''Player:''' Right, right.
