==Making the eggs==
===Correctly===
* {{tcond|Using the dust on the mould:}}
** {{mes|You cover the mould in a layer of chocolate dust.}}
* {{tcond|Using the dusted egg mould on a fire/range:}}
** {{mes|You heat the egg mould.}}
* {{tcond|Emptying the hot egg mould:}}
** {{mes|You pop the warm egg half out of the mould.}}
* {{tcond|Using one egg half on the bucket of freezing milk:}}
** {{mes|I need to stick two halves together before cooling them.}}
* {{tcond|Using one egg half on the other:}}
** {{tbox|pic=Warm easter egg detail.png|The warm chocolate seals the two egg halves together.}}
* {{tcond|Using the warm egg on the freezing milk:}}
** {{mes|You cool the egg with the freezing milk.}}

===Incorrectly===
* {{tcond|Using the dust on the freezing milk:}}
** {{mes|It would be a waste to use these ingredients for chocolate milk.}}
* {{tcond|Using the freezing milk on the mould:}}
** {{mes|Easter eggs are made from chocolate, not milk.}}
* {{tcond|Using the dust on another piece of dust:}}
** {{mes|That would just make a bigger pile of chocolate dust.}}
* {{tcond|Using more dust on the dusted egg mould:}}
** {{mes|The mould is already dusted with chocolate.}}
* {{tcond|Using the freezing milk on the dusted egg mould:}}
** {{mes|That would just wash away the chocolate dust.}}
* {{tcond|Using the dust on the hot egg mould:}}
** {{mes|The mould already has a layer of chocolate in it.}}
* {{tcond|Using the freezing milk on the hot egg mould:}}
** {{mes|The egg half should be removed from the mould before cooling it in the milk.}}
* {{tcond|Emptying the hot egg mould with no inventory space:}}
** {{mes|You need one more inventory space to hold the chocolate egg half.}}
* {{tcond|Using the dust on the egg half:}}
** {{mes|That doesn't need more chocolate adding{{sic}} to it.}}
* {{tcond|Using one egg half on the mould:}}
** {{mes|There is no need to remould the egg half.}}
* {{tcond|Using one egg half on the dusted egg mould:}}
** {{mes|The mould is already dusted with chocolate.}}
* {{tcond|Using the dusted egg mould on the easter egg half:}}
** {{mes|The mould is already dusted in chocolate.}}
* {{tcond|Using one egg half on the hot egg mould:}}
** {{mes|The mould already has a layer of chocolate in it.}}
* {{tcond|Using the dust on the warm egg:}}
** {{mes|That doesn't need more chocolate adding{{sic}} to it.}}
* {{tcond|Using the warm egg on the mould:}}
** {{mes|There is no need to remould the egg.}}
* {{tcond|Using the warm egg on the dusted egg mould:}}
** {{mes|The mould is already dusted with chocolate.}}
* {{tcond|Using the warm egg on the hot egg mould:}}
** {{mes|The mould already has a layer of chocolate in it.}}
* {{tcond|Using another egg half on the warm egg:}}
** {{mes|The egg does not require a third half.}}
* {{tcond|Using another warm egg on the warm egg:}}
** {{mes|No double eggs this year.}}
* {{tcond|Using the dust on the Easter egg:}}
** {{mes|That doesn't need more chocolate adding{{sic}} to it.}}
* {{tcond|Using the freezing milk on the Easter egg:}}
** {{mes|The Easter egg is already cool.}}
* {{tcond|Using the Easter egg on the mould:}}
** {{mes|There is no need to remould the egg.}}
* {{tcond|Using the Easter egg on the dusted egg mould:}}
** {{mes|The mould is already dusted with chocolate.}}
* {{tcond|Using the Easter egg on the hot egg mould:}}
** {{mes|The mould already has a layer of chocolate in it.}}
* {{tcond|Using an egg half on the Easter egg:}}
** {{mes|The egg does not require a third half.}}
* {{tcond|Using the warm egg on the Easter egg:}}
** {{mes|No double eggs this year.}}
* {{tcond|Using another Easter egg on the Easter egg:}}
** {{mes|No double eggs this year.}}
* {{tcond|When Cooking has been drained to 0}}
** {{tbox|You need a Cooking level of 1 to heat the egg mould.}}


