{{Transcript|item}}

{{colour|#00007f|Copied for Guild Records by Scribe Verity.}}

Early numbers suggest that migration is down again this year. The composition remains stable. It's not as if one species has stopped migrating, but all of them are
migrating in lower numbers than before. It may be worth considering a broader guild effort to dig into what's happening here, but for now, I'll be moving toward the pass itself.

{{colour|#00007f|---}}

As yet, I've not observed anything I'd consider to be out of the ordinary within the pass. I'll aim to move a little further up in the coming week if this remains fruitless.

{{colour|#00007f|---}}

Still nothing much of note to document, but the Custodia Pass does seem to now have a relatively high density of rabbits compared to previous reports. I need to identify if they have come from the Auburn Valley, or if we've simply missed a population in our records. I shall attempt to catch a couple and clarify the situation in my next report.

{{colour|#00007f|---}}

Having caught a couple, it is clear that these rabbits are not a part of the Auburn Valley population. The ones I have captured present with what can only be described as fangs. I've never seen anything like it. I will endeavour to learn as much as I can about these rabbits whilst I am here. Expect further reports soon.

