* {{topt|cond=If Mudfoot's Big Adventure is progressed enough:|Could you give me some combat advice?}} <!-- needs confirmation if quest progression is required for this dialogue option to show up -->
** '''Player:''' Could you give me some combat advice?
** '''Captain Harlan:''' Well, first up, there are three types of combat: melee, ranged and magic. Melee uses close up weapons like swords and warhammers, whereas ranged uses things like bows, crossbows or throwing knives.
** '''Captain Harlan:''' Magic is a little different. It's an innate ability, so doesn't actually need any weapons at all. That said, your spells will work better if you channel them using a staff.
** '''Player:''' And the three together make up the combat triangle?
** '''Captain Harlan:''' Indeed. Melee often works best against an opponent using ranged, ranged typically works best when fighting an opponent using magic, and magic is normally the best option when fighting someone using melee.
** '''Captain Harlan:''' Now, that said, do bear in mind that the combat triangle isn't an absolute rule. It's a good starting point, but you will sometimes come across foes that don't follow it.
** '''Player:''' I see. And what about different weapon types?
** '''Captain Harlan:''' Well, there are also many different kinds of weapons, and different ways of using them. Take melee for example. You have crushing attacks, slashing attacks and stabbing attacks.
** '''Captain Harlan:''' Different styles of attack will work better against different types of opponent, but you'll need to make sure you have the right weapon for the job.
** '''Captain Harlan:''' For example, if you want to use a crushing attack, you'll be wanting something like a mace or a warhammer, but if your aim is to stab, a dagger or shortsword will be what you'll need.
** {{tbox|pic=Worn Equipment.png|Different pieces of equipment have different stats, making them effective in different situations. You can view your equipment stats in the Worn Equipment panel.}}
** '''Captain Harlan:''' Many weapons are capable of attacking with multiple styles, but in most cases, one style will be the preferred one. Take a scimitar for example. You can stab with it, but slashing is where it works best.
** {{tbox|pic=Combat icon.png|The same weapon can be used in multiple ways. You can use the attack options in the Combat Options panel to select how you want to use your currently equipped weapon.}}
** {{tbox|pic=Combat icon.png|Different attack options will also grant different types of XP. For example, some options will reward Attack XP when used, whereas others will reward Strength XP. Each attack option shows what XP will be given.}}
** '''Captain Harlan:''' If you find yourself needing a weapon, I do have a few spares. Alternatively, you might want to buy one or make one yourself. The local blacksmith might be able to help with that.
** '''Captain Harlan:''' The last important thing to note is food. It's most likely that when it combat, you're going to take some damage. Make sure to have some food with you so that you can heal yourself. 
** '''Captain Harlan:''' You could just buy some, though you might want to gather and cook it yourself instead. For help with the latter, you might want to speak to the cook in the castle.
** '''Captain Harlan:''' Anyway, I think that covers the basics. I'd say practice is the best way to learn more, though I'm sure there are plenty of other ways for you to learn as well.
** {{tbox|pic=Stats icon.png|To learn more about combat, see the guides for Attack, Strength, Defence, Ranged, Magic, Prayer and Hitpoints in the Skills panel.}}
