* {{topt|Can you give me any farming advice?}}
** '''Player:''' Can you give me any farming advice?
** {{trandom}}
** {{topt|Dialogue 1}}
*** '''Kragen:''' The only way to cure a bush or tree of disease is to prune away the diseased leaves with a pair of secateurs. For all other crops I would just apply some plant-cure.
** {{topt|Dialogue 2}}
*** '''Kragen:''' Tree seeds must be grown in a plantpot of soil into a sapling, and then transferred to a tree patch to continue growing to adulthood.
** {{topt|Dialogue 3}}
*** '''Kragen:''' You can put up to ten potatoes, cabbages or onions in vegetable sacks, although you can't have a mix in the same sack.
** {{topt|Dialogue 4}}
*** '''Kragen:''' You can buy all the farming tools from farming shops, which can be found close to the allotments.
** {{topt|Dialogue 5}}
*** '''Kragen:''' Bittercap mushrooms can only be grown in a special patch in Morytania, near the Mort Myre swamp. There the ground is especially dank and suited to growing poisonous fungii.
** {{topt|Dialogue 6}}
*** '''Kragen:''' Supercompost is far better than normal compost, but more expensive to make. You need to rot the right type of item; show me an item, and I'll tell you if it's super- compostable or not.
** {{topt|Dialogue 7}}
*** '''Kragen:''' There is a special patch for growing Belladonna - I believe that it is somewhere near Draynor Manor, where the ground is a tad 'unblessed'.
** {{topt|Dialogue 8}}
*** '''Kragen:''' Applying compost to a patch will not only reduce the chance that your crops will get diseased, but you will also grow more crops to harvest.
** {{topt|Dialogue 9}}
*** '''Kragen:''' If you want to grow fruit trees you could try a few places: Catherby, Brimhaven, Gnome Stronghold and the Farming Guild all have fruit tree patches.
** {{topt|Dialogue 10}}
*** '''Kragen:''' You can fill plantpots with soil from any empty patch, if you have a gardening trowel.
** {{topt|Dialogue 11}}
*** '''Kragen:''' Hops are good for brewing ales. I believe there's a brewery up in Keldagrim somewhere, and I've heard rumours that a place called Phasmatys used to be good for that type of thing. 'Fore they all died, of course.
** {{topt|Dialogue 12}}
*** '''Kragen:''' Vegetables, hops and flowers need constant watering - if you ignore my advice, you will sooner or later find yourself in possession of a dead farming patch.
** {{topt|Dialogue 13}}
*** '''Kragen:''' You can put up to five tomatoes, strawberries, apples, bananas or oranges into a fruit basket, although you can't have a mix in the same basket.
** {{topt|Dialogue 14}}
*** '''Kragen:''' Don't just throw away your weeds after you've raked a patch - put them in a compost bin and make some compost.
** {{topt|Dialogue 15}}
*** {{tcond|If the player has not finished Song of the Elves:}}
**** '''Kragen:''' There are five other Farming areas like this one - Elstan's area near Falador, Dantaera's area near Catherby, Lyra's area in Morytania, Marisi's area in Hosidius and Alan's area in the Farming Guild.
*** {{tcond|If the player has finished Song of the Elves:}}
**** '''Kragen:''' There are five{{sic|Should say six}} other Farming areas like this one - Elstan's area near Falador, Dantaera's area near Catherby, Lyra's area in Morytania, Marisi's area in Hosidius, Alan's area in the Farming Guild and Oswallt's
**** '''Kragen:''' area in Prifddinas.
** {{topt|Dialogue 16}}
*** '''Kragen:''' If you want to make your own sacks and baskets you'll need to use the loom that's near the Farming shop in Falador. If you're a good enough [craftsman/craftswoman], that is.
** {{topt|Dialogue 17}}
*** '''Kragen:''' You don't have to buy all your plantpots you know, you can make them yourself on a pottery wheel. If you're a good enough [craftsman/craftswoman], that is.
** {{tact|initial}}
