* '''Pious Pete:''' [Brother/Sister] [player name] - welcome to the Realm of Memories. <!--whether he calls you brother or sister is based on body type, not pronouns-->
* {{tselect|Select an option}}
* {{topt|What did you do before you came here?}}
** '''Player:''' What did you do before you came here?
** '''Pious Pete:''' I worked in a chapel dedicated to our lord, Saradomin. My task was to light the chapel candles, but I couldn't reach them myself and I kept getting dazzled by the light whenever I tried.
** '''Pious Pete:''' I'd call adventurers from across the world, summoning them to my chapel to do the task for me. I needed them to light the tall candles, but not the short ones.
** '''Pious Pete:''' However, adventurers got confused, and thought they should light the short candles as well as the tall candles, so I made them try again. And again.
** '''Pious Pete:''' Eventually my chapel was closed down. They said I'd trapped adventurers there for too long. All I wanted was for them to light the tall candles without lighting the short candles!
** '''Pious Pete:''' Anyway, now I live here, and remember the good old days. It is nice to meet you, [player name].
** {{tact|other}}
* {{topt|So your name is Pete?}}
** '''Player:''' So your name is Pete?
** '''Pious Pete:''' Yes, it is a common name. I also know of Party Pete, Parroty Pete, Postie Pete, Pirate Pete, Petrified Pete and 'Picarron' Pete. The Makeover Mage has used the name Pete too.
** '''Pious Pete:''' Although we are not related, the shared bond of that name can be a comfort in dark times.
** {{tact|other}}
* {{topt|cond=After selecting one of the other options:|Goodbye.}}
** '''Player:''' Goodbye.
** {{tact|end}}

{{Transcript|item}}

{{Colour|#600000|*Seemingly written by Erysail the Pious, this book details some of the more monotonous parts of the lives of the Seven Priestly Warriors, the oaths they've sworn, and more... The book remains a largely factual account, but on one page, a more opinionated view comes across.*}}

The Temple Knights are to be made up of the most devout followers of Saradomin. How else could they be trusted to bring about his will? One would have to be naive to think that anybody else could truly understand the purpose we're serving.

Twiblick was said to be converted. We were clearly told this when questions were first raised of a Taverley born druid joining the organisation. However, the different prayers that he speaks as every night comes, clutching his Guthixian charms, seem to tell a different story. The more likely explanation seems to be what I heard whispered, that he was just too good to turn down. Saradomin's warriors would surely have been enough though, without relying on this outside help.

Still, it does seem that he is worthy of some grace... Whether or not he should have been initiated in the first place, and while we don't quite see eye to eye, Friar certainly has been a useful addition to this operation.

