{{Transcript|npc}}
==Standard dialogue==
* '''Player:''' Hey there, is this where you live?
* '''Poor looking man:''' Yes it is! Don't look down your nose at me. I have to put up with an awful lot to earn my living, life is a daily struggle.
* '''Player:''' Sorry, I am just curious. Why is life so difficult here?
* {{trandom}}
* {{topt|Dialogue 1}}
** '''Poor looking man:''' Just look at the place, rats, flies and all sorts just swarming the area. Doesn't help that I stink but ain't no one who likes using those tin baths right in public view.
** {{tact|end}}
* {{topt|Dialogue 2}}
** '''Poor looking man:''' It is difficult to make ends meet. There are just so many skilled fishermen here that the competition is too much! Leaves no room for someone like me.
** {{tact|end}}
* {{topt|Dialogue 3}}
** '''Poor looking man:''' Thieves! Thieves everywhere. Come to think of it, they always look remarkably like you! Adventurers running about stealing our things, get out of my sight.
** {{tact|end}}
* {{topt|Dialogue 4}}
** '''Poor looking man:''' Look, this is none of your business, I'd appreciate it if you left me to it. I don't want to see another fancy adventurer again!
** '''Player:''' Okay okay! I'll be off now.
** {{tact|end}}
* {{topt|Dialogue 5}}
** '''Poor looking man:''' Gang crime is everywhere! I see them sometimes... it makes me very uneasy. It becomes difficult to sleep at night, never mind the draft in here.
** '''Player:''' I've heard about those gangs! The Shayzien soldiers do a lot of work to put an end to it.
** '''Poor looking man:''' Don't talk to me about those soldiers, all they ever do is blitz onto these docks with not a care in the world for us folk.
** {{tact|end}}

