==Standard dialogue==
* '''Ranged combat tutor:''' Hey there adventurer, I am the Ranged combat tutor. Is there anything you would like to know?
* {{topt|How can I train my Ranged?}}
** '''Player:''' How can I train my Ranged?
** {{tcond|If the player's Ranged level is below 29 :}}
*** '''Ranged combat tutor:''' To start with you'll need a bow and arrows, you were given a Shortbow and some arrows when you arrived here from Tutorial island.
*** '''Ranged combat tutor:''' Alternatively, you can claim a training bow and some arrows from me.
*** '''Ranged combat tutor:''' Mikasi, the Magic Combat tutor and I both give out items every 30 minutes, however you must choose whether you want runes or ranged equipment.
*** '''Ranged combat tutor:''' To claim the Training bow and arrows, right-click on me and choose Claim, to claim runes right-click on the Magic Combat tutor and select Claim.
*** {{tact|opens=Skills}}
*** '''Ranged combat tutor:''' Not all bows can use every type of arrow, most bows have a limit. You can find out your bows limit by checking the Ranged skill guide.
*** '''Ranged combat tutor:''' If you do decide to use the Training bow, you will only be able to use the Training arrows with it. Remember to pick up your arrows, re-use them and come back when you need more.
*** '''Ranged combat tutor:''' Once you have your bow and arrows, equip them by selecting their Wield option in your inventory.
*** {{tact|opens=Combat options}}
*** '''Ranged combat tutor:''' You can change the way you attack by going to the combat options tab. There are three attack styles for bows. Those styles are Accurate, Rapid and Longrange.
*** '''Ranged combat tutor:''' Accurate increases your bows attack accuracy. Rapid will increase your attack speed with the bow. Longrange will let you attack your enemies from a greater distance.
*** {{tcond|If the player is eligible for [[Adventure paths]]:}}
**** '''Ranged combat tutor:''' If you need some more advice, you should talk to Adventurer Jon about Adventure paths. He may even have a handy starter kit you can use.
**** {{tact|continue}}
*** {{tact|continue}}
** {{tcond|If the player's Ranged level is 29 to 43:}}
*** '''Ranged combat tutor:''' Use the best bow and arrows you can get your hands on and practically use, for your level. This will ensure maximum damage.
*** '''Ranged combat tutor:''' Choose carefully where you shoot from. If you can, use fences and other things to help protect you whilst you fight.
*** '''Ranged combat tutor:''' You may also find that the better the ranged armour you use, the more accurate you will be with your bow.
*** '''Ranged combat tutor:''' If you are ever in the market for a new bow or some arrows, you should head on over to Lowe's Archery Emporium in Varrock. I can show you where the shop is if you like.
*** {{topt|Yes please.}}
**** '''Player:''' Yes please.
**** {{tact|The world map opens and pans to the location of [[Lowe's Archery Emporium]].}}
*** {{topt|No thanks.}}
**** '''Player:''' No thanks{{sic}}
**** '''Ranged combat tutor:''' Is there anything else you want to know?
**** {{tact|other}}
** {{tcond|If the player's Ranged level is 44 or above:}}
*** {{tcond|If the player's Ranged level is 99}}:
**** '''Ranged combat tutor:''' My word, I think you should be the one giving me advice instead, but I will do my best.
**** {{tact|continue}}
*** '''Ranged combat tutor:''' You should know the basics of ranged combat by now, but if you are looking for somewhere to test your skills and make some money, you should try hunting Moss giants in Varrock sewers.
*** '''Ranged combat tutor:''' If you are lucky you might find a Mossy key, with this key you will be able to enter Bryophyta's lair. Make sure to bring plenty of food and good armour and weapons when you fight her as you will need it.
*** '''Ranged combat tutor:''' If your{{sic}} lucky you might snag some goodies that you can sell for a decent profit.
*** '''Ranged combat tutor:''' If you are looking to do something different, visit the ranging guild over near Hemenster, there you can practice your archery and earn tickets for it at the same time.
*** '''Ranged combat tutor:''' You can then hand those tickets in for a variety of goods you can use to train your Ranged skill.
*** {{tact|continue}}
** '''Ranged combat tutor:''' If you are ever in the market for a new bow or some arrows, you should head on over to Lowe's Archery Emporium in Varrock. I can show you where the shop is if you like.
** {{topt|Yes please.}}
*** {{tact|The world map opens and pans to the location of [[Lowe's Archery Emporium]].}}
** {{topt|No thanks.}}
*** '''Player:''' No thanks{{sic}}
*** '''Ranged combat tutor:''' Is there anything else you want to know?
*** {{tact|other}}
* {{topt|How do I create a bow and arrows?}}
** '''Ranged combat tutor:''' Ahh the art of fletching. Fletching is used to create your own bow and arrows.
** {{tcond|If the player is on a free-to-play world:}}
*** '''Ranged combat tutor:''' To create your bow and arrows you would need to gather some wood, feathers, arrow heads and bow string. The wood would be to make arrow shafts which can be turned into unstrung bows and arrow shafts.
*** '''Ranged combat tutor:''' Unfortunately, Fletching is a member only skill so you will have to get your ranging supplies from shops or other players.
*** '''Ranged combat tutor:''' Is there anything else you want to know?
*** {{tact|other}}
** {{tcond|If the player is on a members' world:}}
*** '''Ranged combat tutor:''' It's quite simple really. You'll need an axe to cut some logs from trees and a knife. Knives can be found in and around the Lumbridge castle and in the Varrock General store upstairs.
*** '''Ranged combat tutor:''' Use your knife on the logs. This will bring up a menu listing items you can fletch.
*** '''Ranged combat tutor:''' For arrows you will need to smith some arrow heads and kill some chickens for feathers.
*** '''Ranged combat tutor:''' Add the feathers to your Arrow shafts to make Headless arrows, then use your chosen arrow heads on the Headless arrows to make your arrows.
*** '''Ranged combat tutor:''' Now for making bows. When accessing the fletching menu, instead of choosing Arrows shafts, you can make an unstrung bow instead.
*** '''Ranged combat tutor:''' To complete the bow you will need to get your hands on a Bow string.
*** '''Ranged combat tutor:''' First you will need to get some flax from a flax field. There's one south of Seers' Village. Gather flax, then spin it on a spinning wheel, there's one in Seers' Village too.
*** '''Ranged combat tutor:''' This makes bow strings which you can then use on the unstrung bows to make a working bow!
*** '''Player:''' Brilliant. If I forget anything I'll come talk to you again.
*** '''Ranged combat tutor:''' Is there anything else you want to know?
*** {{tact|other}}
* {{topt|Can you toggle my ammo to equip when I pick it up please?}}
** '''Ranged combat tutor:''' Certainly. If you pick up ammo that is the same ammo you are currently using, I can make that ammo automatically equip for you, providing you have space of course!
** '''Ranged combat tutor:''' Or you can leave it to going into your inventory like normal.
** {{tselect|How do you want to handle picking up ammo?}}
*** {{topt|Automatically equip it.}}
**** '''Ranged combat tutor:''' There you go! Your ammo will now automatically be equipped when you pick it up.
**** '''Ranged combat tutor:''' Is there anything else you want to know?
**** {{tact|initial}}
*** {{topt|Place it in my inventory.}}
**** '''Ranged combat tutor:''' There you go! Your ammo will now go to your inventory when you pick it up.
**** '''Ranged combat tutor:''' Is there anything else you want to know?
**** {{tact|initial}}
* {{topt|Goodbye.}}
** '''Player:''' Goodbye.
** {{tact|end}}

