{{Transcript|item}}

{{Colour|#600000|*This book seems to have been used for the writings of Friar Twiblick. Rather than a biographical journal, it seems Friar instead took pride in filling it with anecdotal thoughts and his day to day musings. However, one particular entry catches your eye.*}}

I always thought that the Temple Knights were bound to be clean shaven. I never quite knew why, or if it was a truly written rule for that matter, but I'd been under that impression all the same...

Taverley was never the warmest town, but the difference here is much bigger than I'd expected. As the nights get longer, the days are sure enough getting colder, and even those little bits of warmth go a long way. The breeze from across the Salve is starting to get to me, and that bushy rug on Derygull's face sure does seem comforting right about now!

Ah well, lesson learnt for the next mission, I suppose.

