===Corporal Breiman===
* '''Corporal Breiman:''' How goes it? You're the one doing some of your own investigating, right?
* '''Player:''' That's right.
* '''Corporal Breiman:''' Pleased to meet you. I'm Corporal Michael Breiman. I work with Corporal Campter and Sergeant Hudson.
* '''Player:''' And you guys at the ones who investigate things like this?
* '''Corporal Breiman:''' Like murder? Yup, that's our domain. Very cheery.
* '''Corporal Breiman:''' We work for the Shayzien Constabulary. It's part of the Shayzien Military. We investigate crimes all across the kingdom.
* '''Player:''' I see. What are your thoughts so far?
* '''Corporal Breiman:''' Well, it's still a bit early to suggest too much. That said, this one doesn't look good.
* '''Player:''' Do any murders look good?
* '''Corporal Breiman:''' Well... No, but this one could be particularly nasty. You see, there are generally three kinds of murder.
* '''Corporal Breiman:''' First, you've got your petty crime that gets out of hand. Thievery and the like. From time to time, a thief ends up biting off more than they can chew, and the victim fights back.
* '''Corporal Breiman:''' Both parties panic in that situation, and it sometimes ends badly.
* '''Corporal Breiman:''' Then you've got your domestic violence. An argument breaks out between the victim and someone close to them and it spirals out of control. It's by far the most common type of murder we see.
* '''Corporal Breiman:''' Now, the thing about those first two is that the killer never sets out to kill someone. One thing leads to another and then there's a body on the floor. That's what's so dangerous about the third kind.
* '''Corporal Breiman:''' You see, with the third kind of murder, the killer wants the victim dead. They plan for it, sometimes for months. They set out with the intention of ending someone's life.
* '''Player:''' And you think that's what we're dealing with here?
* '''Corporal Breiman:''' It definitely looks that way. Our victim here was a bit of a public figure before he retired. I even remember hearing stories about him when I was a kid.
* '''Corporal Breiman:''' That, combined with the lovely decoration on the wall, and the way the victim's been dismembered... Well, it doesn't paint a good picture...
* '''Corporal Breiman:''' Anyway, I'll let you get on with your investigation. If you need anything, just let me or my partner know. She should be outside somewhere.
* '''Player:''' Will do. Thanks.
* {{tact|end}}

===Corporal Campter===
* '''Player:''' Hello there.
* '''Corporal Campter:''' Hello, citizen. I hear you're going to be doing some investigating with us.
* '''Player:''' That's right. Not that your boss seemed very happy about it.
* '''Corporal Campter:''' Ah, don't worry about him. He can be a bit short with people sometimes. It's how he is when he's in his thinking mode.
* '''Player:''' Thinking mode?
* '''Corporal Campter:''' That's right. He's the brains of the operation you see. I'm Corporal Sarah Campter. It's my job, along with my partner, to gather up any evidence and interview the witnesses.
* '''Corporal Campter:''' Once we've done that, we present it to the Sergeant and he pieces it all together. He's caught more killers than you could count!
* '''Player:''' I see. So, any tips for my investigation?
* '''Corporal Campter:''' Well, when it comes to murder, there are a few things we generally look at. First, there's the body itself. Determining the cause of death is a good start for any investigation.
* '''Corporal Campter:''' After that, there's searching the crime scene, or any other areas of interest. We look for anything the killer might have left behind, but also possible hints at a motive that could be hidden amongst the victim's possessions.
* '''Corporal Campter:''' Finally, the witnesses. We'll interview anyone who we think might have seen something, or who might have had contact with the victim before their death. Neighbours... family... Those kinds of people,
* '''Corporal Campter:''' They can often fill in critical gaps in the evidence, but be careful. Even when not guilty, people have a habit of telling lies.
* '''Player:''' I see. Thanks for the help.
* '''Corporal Campter:''' Don't mention it. If you need anything else, my partner should be over in the house. He might have some useful information for you.
* {{tact|end}}

