* '''Familiar Voice:''' Get up.
* '''Betty:''' I said get up.
* '''Player:''' Betty...? What is this...?
* '''Betty:''' You should know what this is... You investigated it. All those clues... and you still couldn't work it out.
* '''Player:''' It was... It was you!
* '''Betty:''' Of course it was me. Who else could it have been?
* '''Player:''' But... your own father... Why?
* '''Betty:''' Because he was a monster! For my entire childhood we lived in fear of him, until the day finally came when my mother decided enough was enough...
* '''Betty:''' But he couldn't allow that! He couldn't let her be free. That's why he poisoned her! Her and my sister!
* '''Betty:''' Then, with a little help from his Keystone Lodge friends, he had it all covered up!
* '''Betty:''' But now, after all these years, it's finally over! They're finally dead! All that remains now, is you.
* '''Player:''' Me? Why? I tried to help you!
* '''Betty:''' But you never once looked deeper! Don't you see? You're just as big a part of the problem as they were!
* '''Betty:''' People like them... the only reason they get away with the things they do is because people like you stand by and let them!
* '''Betty:''' You never really cared! You people never do! This was all just a bit of fun to you. But now the fun is over...
* '''Sergeant Hudson:''' Indeed it is.
* {{qact|The three Shayzien soldiers arrive.}}
* '''Betty:''' What...? How?!
* '''Sergeant Hudson:''' By following the clues, Betty. Isn't that what you wanted?
* '''Betty:''' But you never even cared!
* '''Sergeant Hudson:''' Oh I very much did. That's why one of the first things I did was look into the death of your mother and sister. The investigation into their deaths was quite thorough...
* '''Sergeant Hudson:''' The conclusion? An illness. One so tragic, the surviving daughter never fully recovered. She spent years in care, but eventually her father decided to bring her home.
* '''Sergeant Hudson:''' He was advised against it. She was unpredictable. Sometimes even violent. But he insisted.
* '''Betty:''' You're lying!
* '''Sergeant Hudson:''' The people you killed were innocent, Betty. No one is to blame for what happened to your mother and sister. You've just never been able to accept that.
* '''Sergeant Hudson:''' Now, I think it's time to bring this madness to an end. You're coming with us, Betty.
* '''Betty:''' So you can execute me in front of a cheering crowd? Or lock me in a cell to live the rest of my life with no sunlight and a diet of mouldy bread? No. This ends here!
* {{qact|Betty stabs herself and dies.}}
* '''Sergeant Hudson:''' *sigh*
* '''Sergeant Hudson:''' Come on, adventurer, let's get you out of here. Corporals... get started on cleaning up here.
* {{qact|The cutscene ends.}}
* '''Sergeant Hudson:''' Well... This one is going to have some paperwork to deal with...
* '''Player:''' When did you realise?
* '''Sergeant Hudson:''' Hmm?
* '''Player:''' That it was Betty.
* '''Sergeant Hudson:''' She was a prime suspect from the start. Such is always the case when dealing with a murder. In the vast majority of cases, the killer and the victim know each other.
* '''Sergeant Hudson:''' As for when I knew for sure, I had a strong hunch, but it was just that until you led us to her.
* '''Player:''' It would have been nice of you to tell me...
* '''Sergeant Hudson:''' Yes, it would have been, but through your own choices, you made yourself a suspect as well. It's nothing personal, but that is the way of things I'm afraid.
* '''Player:''' I suppose...
* '''Sergeant Hudson:''' If it makes you feel better, your work did end up being useful. You found a couple of things we missed, and you did a good job piecing everything together.
* '''Sergeant Hudson:''' I can't offer you much as thanks, but I do have an amulet here that might be useful to you.
* '''Sergeant Hudson:''' Now, I'd best get to work. We have a lot of tidying up to do. All the best, adventurer.
