*** '''Town crier:''' put them straight!
** {{topt|Dialogue 10}}
*** '''Town crier:''' Have the P-Mod Oracle open in a separate window when playing Old School RuneScape - that way you'll always have the most up-to-date guidelines to hand!
** {{topt|Dialogue 11}}
*** '''Town crier:''' If the chat is scrolling too fast for you to see that suspect line you want to double check, just run up a ladder or to a quieter spot to stop the chat screen scrolling. Then you can scroll back and read that
*** '''Town crier:''' suspect line and judge the situation in your own time!
** {{topt|Dialogue 12}}
*** '''Town crier:''' If the chat window is moving too quickly to report a player accurately, run to a quiet spot and review the chat at your leisure!
** {{topt|Dialogue 13}}
*** '''Town crier:''' If a player isn't sure of the rules, send them to me! I'll be happy to remind them!
** {{topt|Dialogue 14}}
*** '''Town crier:''' If you're a new mod, don't forget to read the guidelines before you log into the game! If you've been a P-mod for a while, why not have another read of them to refresh your memory and to get up to date
*** '''Town crier:''' with any changes you may have missed!
** {{topt|Dialogue 15}}
*** '''Town crier:''' If you've got a player asking you questions about P- mods, feel free to send them to me; I can answer questions about P-mods for you!
** {{topt|Dialogue 16}}
*** '''Town crier:''' If you get harassed by a player in game, don't take it personally - the player is reacting to your silver crown, not to you!
** {{topt|Dialogue 17}}
*** '''Town crier:''' If you notice a player trying to buy something common for an extremely high price, look about and see if there's someone else selling the same item for a much lower price. Chances are they're team scamming. If so,
*** '''Town crier:''' write their names down and send your J-mod curators a query!
** {{topt|Dialogue 18}}
*** '''Town crier:''' If you see a player abusing a bug in game, there's no need to report the player, just submit a bug report via the in-game report form.
** {{topt|Dialogue 19}}
*** '''Town crier:''' An important part of being a P-mod is to act as an ambassador for the game. Keeping your cool even when faced with the rudest players goes a long way towards this!
** {{topt|Dialogue 20}}
*** '''Town crier:''' It's always better to report in secret. Telling a player that you are about to report them rarely makes you a friend, and can often lead to a player being offensive to you!
** {{topt|Dialogue 21}}
*** '''Town crier:''' Make sure you log out of the game and the forums whenever you leave your device. Don't allow others to see confidential info!
** {{topt|Dialogue 22}}
*** '''Town crier:''' Never answer questions if you feel the answer will breach confidentiality.
** {{topt|Dialogue 23}}
*** '''Town crier:''' The P-mod forums are your friend! They're the best place to talk to and meet other P-mods and are absolutely packed with useful advice!
** {{topt|Dialogue 24}}
*** '''Town crier:''' Remember, if in doubt, report without a mute! It's very frustrating not to be able to speak if you're innocent!
** {{topt|Dialogue 25}}
*** '''Town crier:''' Remember, if offensive language has been completely filtered out then there's no need to report or mute it!
** {{topt|Dialogue 26}}
*** '''Town crier:''' Think twice before applying that mute. Will it really prevent further damage from surrounding players?
** {{topt|Dialogue 27}}
*** '''Town crier:''' Use the Jagex PMod team if you need to - they're there to help!
** {{topt|Dialogue 28}}
*** '''Town crier:''' You'll be amazed how often a bit of humour can diffuse a potentially unpleasant situation, before it becomes too serious.
** {{topt|Dialogue 29}}
*** '''Town crier:''' Your J-mods are there to help you. If you ever need their advice, send them a query. They are always very happy to help. Don't be afraid to use them!
