==Using items on Wise Old Man==
* {{tcond|If the player has not gone through the initial dialogue first:}}
** '''Wise Old Man:''' Humph! You could at least say hello before waving your items in my face.
** {{tact|end}}

===Item with offensive stats===
* '''Player:''' Do you think I need to keep this?
* '''Wise Old Man:''' I suppose you could use that in combat.
* '''Player:''' Thanks, old man.
* {{tact|end}}

===Item with only defensive stats===
* '''Player:''' Do you think I need to keep this?
* '''Wise Old Man:''' I suppose you could use that for defense.
* '''Player:''' Thanks, old man.
* {{tact|end}}

===Low-value runes===
* '''Player:''' Do you think I need to keep this?
* ''(Wise Old Man takes five runes from you.)''
* '''Wise Old Man:''' Runes are very useful things, but I'll take some of those off your hands for you.
* {{tact|end}}

===High-value runes===
* '''Player:''' Do you think I need to keep this?
* '''Wise Old Man:''' Ooh, runes? Yes, they're quite valuable.
* {{tact|end}}

===Coins===
* '''Player:''' Do you think I need to keep this?
* '''Wise Old Man:''' That's called 'money'. Money is fantastically important if you haven't got enough of it, but when you've got as much as I have, you realise that money doesn't matter.
* '''Player:''' Right...
* {{tact|end}}

===[[Book on chickens]], [[Book of folklore]], or [[Strange book]]===
* '''Player:''' Do you think I need to keep this?
* '''Wise Old Man:''' That's mine. I'll take it back, thank you very much!
* ''(Wise Old Man takes all copies of any of the three books from your inventory)''
* {{tact|end}}

===The [[Banker's briefcase]]===
* '''Wise Old Man:''' How did you get your hands on that?!
* '''Wise Old Man:''' Get out of here this instant.
* {{tact|end}}

===Items with no information===
* '''Player:''' Do you think I need to keep this?
* '''Wise Old Man:''' Tell you what, rather than you showing me items individually, I'll look through all your possessions to see if I can find anything worth discarding.
* {{tact|(Game opens the [[Wise Old Man/Recycling Centre|Wise Old Man's Recycling Center]] interface)}}

==Searching through his bookcases without having talked to him first==
* '''Wise Old Man:''' It'd be politer to come and talk to me before you start messing around with my possessions!
* {{tact|end}}

==After observing his telescope==
* '''Player:''' I see you've got your telescope pointing at the Wizards' Tower.
* '''Wise Old Man:''' Oh, do I? Well, why does that interest you?
* {{tcond|If the player has not seen the bank robbery cutscene:}}
** '''Player:''' It just seems a bit odd.
** '''Wise Old Man:''' Odd? There's nothing odd about a fascination with the magical arts. Besides, the architecture of that Tower is truly remarkable, for one who studies such things.
** '''Player:''' So you're not planning to attack the Tower?
** '''Wise Old Man:''' No, I wouldn't dream of doing anything of the sort!
** '''Player:''' Hmmm...
** {{tact|end}}
* {{tcond|If the player has seen the bank robbery cutscene:}}
** '''Player:''' Well, you robbed a bank, and I bet you're now planning something to do with that Tower!
** '''Wise Old Man:''' No, no. I'm not planning anything like that again.
** '''Player:''' Well I'll be watching you...
** {{tact|end}}

===If the Wise Old Man is in the [[Old Man's coffin]]===
* '''Player:''' Oh, he's not here.
* {{tact|end}}

